WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.407
In under two minutes, you will change your contest's dates and details.

00:00:04.407 --> 00:00:05.520
We start on the map.

00:00:06.421 --> 00:00:09.753
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:13.941
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.941 --> 00:00:16.431
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.431 --> 00:00:17.777
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.746
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.746 --> 00:00:22.398
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:28.423
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.423 --> 00:00:29.640
See the three dots?

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.188
Tap them.

00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:33.754
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:36.082
Tap Mine.

00:00:36.082 --> 00:00:38.030
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:41.729
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:43.097
This is your dashboard.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.278
On the Overview, find Schedule.

00:00:47.278 --> 00:00:48.498
Tap Change dates.

00:00:50.377 --> 00:00:53.559
Change the date that entries close, and the voting dates.

00:00:57.228 --> 00:01:01.400
You can also change the name, the message, the prize, and the rules.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.335
Entrants see changes right away.

00:01:04.236 --> 00:01:05.462
Tap Save changes.

00:01:05.462 --> 00:01:09.414
The team is emailed about changes, so nobody is surprised.

00:01:11.344 --> 00:01:13.213
Next up: Run voting.
